    <div class="tcard"><div class="tcard-img" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#2C3E7A,#1A2550);"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:100%;opacity:0.4"><pattern id="tp2" x="0" y="0" width="30" height="30" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><rect width="30" height="30" fill="none" stroke="#C47A2B" stroke-width="0.4"/></pattern><rect width="300" height="220" fill="url(#tp2)"/></svg><div style="position:absolute;bottom:1rem;left:1rem;font-size:2.5rem;">🏛️</div></div><div class="tcard-body"><div class="tcard-ctry">Italy · Emilia-Romagna</div><h2 class="tcard-city">Bologna</h2><p class="tcard-desc">40km of covered walkways — the world's longest arcaded streetscape — as an urban design lesson in public-private space and climate adaptation predating the concept by 600 years.</p><div class="tcard-tags"><span class="ttag">Arcades</span><span class="ttag">Historic Centre</span><span class="ttag">Walkability</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="tcard"><div class="tcard-img" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--terracotta),var(--mud));"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:100%;opacity:0.4"><pattern id="tp3" x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M12 0 L24 12 L12 24 L0 12 Z" fill="none" stroke="#F0D080" stroke-width="0.4"/></pattern><rect width="300" height="220" fill="url(#tp3)"/></svg><div style="position:absolute;bottom:1rem;left:1rem;font-size:2.5rem;">🌊</div></div><div class="tcard-body"><div class="tcard-ctry">Portugal · Atlantic Coast</div><h2 class="tcard-city">Lisbon & Porto</h2><p class="tcard-desc">Two cities navigating the same tension: spectacular heritage versus tourism pressure, gentrification, and housing unaffordability. The azulejo tiles are gorgeous; the displacement is real.</p><div class="tcard-tags"><span class="ttag">Heritage</span><span class="ttag">Gentrification</span><span class="ttag">Coastal City</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="tcard"><div class="tcard-img" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--leaf),#2A4020);"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:100%;opacity:0.4"><pattern id="tp4" x="0" y="0" width="20" height="34.6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><polygon points="10,0 20,17.3 10,34.6 0,17.3" fill="none" stroke="#F0D080" stroke-width="0.4"/></pattern><rect width="300" height="220" fill="url(#tp4)"/></svg><div style="position:absolute;bottom:1rem;left:1rem;font-size:2.5rem;">⛩️</div></div><div class="tcard-body"><div class="tcard-ctry">Japan · Kansai</div><h2 class="tcard-city">Kyoto & Osaka</h2><p class="tcard-desc">Japan's approach to urban heritage preservation — rigorous, obsessive — set against Osaka's gleeful maximalism. Two cities, 40 minutes apart, with almost nothing in common.</p><div class="tcard-tags"><span class="ttag">Heritage Policy</span><span class="ttag">Urban Contrast</span><span class="ttag">Transit</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="tcard"><div class="tcard-img" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#5A3A6A,#2C3E7A);"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:100%;opacity:0.4"><pattern id="tp5" x="0" y="0" width="32" height="32" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><circle cx="16" cy="16" r="12" fill="none" stroke="#E8621A" stroke-width="0.4"/></pattern><rect width="300" height="220" fill="url(#tp5)"/></svg><div style="position:absolute;bottom:1rem;left:1rem;font-size:2.5rem;">🌙</div></div><div class="tcard-body"><div class="tcard-ctry">Morocco · Atlantic</div><h2 class="tcard-city">Marrakech & Fès</h2><p class="tcard-desc">The Arab-Berber medina as urban laboratory: a city designed entirely for pedestrians, organised by craft guild — a system modern planners still struggle to understand or replicate.</p><div class="tcard-tags"><span class="ttag">Medina</span><span class="ttag">Pedestrian City</span><span class="ttag">Islamic Urbanism</span></div></div></div>
    <div class="tcard"><div class="tcard-img" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--copper),var(--terracotta));"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:100%;opacity:0.4"><pattern id="tp6" x="0" y="0" width="40" height="40" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><rect x="5" y="5" width="30" height="30" fill="none" stroke="#2A1A0E" stroke-width="0.5"/></pattern><rect width="300" height="220" fill="url(#tp6)"/></svg><div style="position:absolute;bottom:1rem;left:1rem;font-size:2.5rem;">🏗️</div></div><div class="tcard-body"><div class="tcard-ctry">India · Maharashtra</div><h2 class="tcard-city">Mumbai</h2><p class="tcard-desc">The most extreme urban density outside Hong Kong. Dharavi as misunderstood city-within-a-city; the Gothic Revival station as monument to colonial ambition; the mill district transformation.</p><div class="tcard-tags"><span class="ttag">Density</span><span class="ttag">Informal Urbanism</span><span class="ttag">Colonial Heritage</span></div></div></div>
